{
  "tema": 6508,
  "slug": "acabar-de-infinitivo",
  "titulo": "Acabar de + infinitive",
  "subtitulo": "Acabo de llegar.",
  "foto": "t08.jpg",
  "regla": "Acabar de + infinitive means to have just done something. Spanish uses the present (acabo de llegar = I've just arrived) where English uses just + past.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Acabar de** + infinitive = _to have just done_ something."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "acabar (present)",
            "+ de +",
            "infinitive"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "English says _I just arrived_ or _I've just arrived_; Spanish uses the **present** of acabar: **acabo de llegar**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "acabar de"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "acabo de"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "acabas de"
            ],
            [
              "él, ella, usted",
              "acaba de"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros/as",
              "acabamos de"
            ],
            [
              "ellos, ellas, ustedes",
              "acaban de"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Object and reflexive pronouns go before acabar or stuck to the infinitive: **lo acabo de ver** = **acabo de verlo**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Careful: in the preterite, **acabé de comer** means _I finished eating_, not _I just ate_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **acabo de** is the wet footprint on the floor. You're not in the shower anymore, but you only just got out."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==Acabo de== salir del agua.",
              "en": "I've just got out of the water."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Acabamos de== comer.",
              "en": "We've just eaten."
            },
            {
              "es": "Lupita ==acaba de== mandarte un mensaje.",
              "en": "Lupita just sent you a message."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Te ==acabas de== despertar?",
              "en": "Did you just wake up?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Los vecinos ==acaban de== plantar unos jitomates.",
              "en": "The neighbors have just planted some tomatoes."
            },
            {
              "es": "El partido ==acaba de== terminar.",
              "en": "The game has just ended."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Lo acabo de== ver en la playa.",
              "en": "I just saw him at the beach."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Acabé de llegar. (= I just arrived)"
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Acabo de llegar."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "_Just_: present **acabo**."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Acabo llegar."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Acabo de llegar."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Don't drop **de**."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Acabo de llegado."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Acabo de llegar."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Infinitive, not participle."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Solo llegué."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Acabo de llegar."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "_Just_ here isn't **solo**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
